    "finding_info": {
        "uid": "placeholder_uid",
        "title": "LockBit 4.0 Ransomware Encryption Behavior Detected and Killed",
        "desc": "The SentinelOne agent on ws-fin-042.contoso.corp observed a high-confidence behavioral chain matching LockBit 4.0 ransomware. The process svchost_helper.exe (parent: rundll32.exe) rapidly enumerated user document directories, deleted volume shadow copies via vssadmin.exe delete shadows /all /quiet, disabled Windows Recovery via bcdedit.exe /set {default} recoveryenabled No, and began renaming files with the .lockbit4 extension while writing ransom notes named !!!-Restore-My-Files-!!!.txt to every touched directory. The Storyline engine linked the process tree back to an initial-access LNK executed by the user 12 minutes earlier. The threat was auto-mitigated: process killed, files rolled back from local cache, and the endpoint quarantined from the network. MITRE ATT&CK: T1486 (Data Encrypted for Impact), T1490 (Inhibit System Recovery), T1489 (Service Stop), T1059.003 (Windows Command Shell)."
    },
